"site.help.changelog.expandingLandCinematicDeath": "<strong>Expanding Land Cinematic Death & FX Pipeline</strong> — integrated client-side cinematic death sequence into standard packet handlers. Includes particle bursts, eater pulse effect, camera screen shake, and 600ms player absorption animation.",
"site.help.changelog.virusJellyPhysicsUpdated": "<strong>Virus Jelly Physics</strong> — updated virus renderer to support dynamic jelly spring physics while maintaining jagged spike boundaries.",
"site.help.changelog.clientConnectionSkinLoading": "<strong>Client Connection & Skin Loading Stability</strong> — added backoff/capping on auto-reconnect loops, color gradient fallbacks for missing skins, and lock protection against grey transit cells.",
"site.help.changelog.april2026": "April 2026",
"site.help.changelog.fixedSpectatorCellColor": "<strong>Fixed spectator cell color mismatch</strong> — spectators could see a player's cells rendered with different colors after a skin loaded via login. Root cause: <code>server_invalidate_player_cells()</code> only invalidated active (alive) players' view caches, never touching spectator view state (<code>spec_view_state</code>, <code>center_spec_view_state</code>). Old cells kept the no-skin appearance while new splits showed the skin, creating a two-tone visual",
"site.help.changelog.invalidationNowCoversAll": "Invalidation now covers all three viewer paths: individual (alive + free-roam spectators via <code>connected_ids</code>), grouped spectators, and center spectators",
"site.help.changelog.alsoClearsViewState": "Also clears <code>view_state[]</code> when removing cells from <code>client_nodes</code>, ensuring the diff engine classifies re-added cells as ADD (with full skin/name) instead of UPDATE",
"site.help.changelog.performance": "Performance",
"site.help.changelog.deferredViewStateClearing": "<strong>Deferred view_state clearing</strong> — <code>server_remove_cell()</code> no longer iterates all connected players to clear visibility state per removal. Clearing is deferred to <code>server_alloc_cell()</code> at reuse time. Eliminates O(connected × removed) random cache-cold writes per tick",
"site.help.changelog.singleQuadtreeRebuildPer": "<strong>Single quadtree rebuild per tick</strong> — merged the two separate <code>server_rebuild_quadtree()</code> calls (post-movement and post-spawn) into a single rebuild after all mutations are complete. Saves ~0.3–0.5ms per tick at 5000+ dynamic cells",
"site.help.changelog.incrementalFoodGridAdded": "<strong>Incremental food grid</strong> — added <code>fg_remove()</code> for O(1) bucket removal. Food eat/spawn now use incremental insert/remove instead of triggering a full rebuild of 4000+ entries. Full rebuild only triggers on border change (map resize)",
"site.help.changelog.ejectedRigidBodyEarly": "<strong>Ejected rigid body early-out</strong> — the ejected-vs-ejected push-apart loop now skips entirely when <code>moving_count == 0</code> (no cells in flight). Avoids scanning all dynamic_nodes on quiet ticks",
"site.help.changelog.antiTeamingSystemRewritten": "<strong>Anti-teaming system rewritten</strong> — replaced the legacy discrete event-based system (64-event array per player, 788 bytes/player) with a Delta Server-style exponential decay multiplier (single float, 8 bytes). Each teaming action bumps a multiplier; decay = base × pow(1.086, multiplier). Recovery is automatic via a compensation constant (-0.005/cycle). ~780 bytes saved per player (~3MB for 3840 players).",
"site.help.changelog.newConfigParametersAt": "New config parameters: <code>at_extra_decay_base</code>, <code>at_compensation</code>, <code>at_split_loss</code>, <code>at_eject_loss</code>, <code>at_virus_pop_loss</code>, <code>at_danger_loss</code>",
"site.help.changelog.opcode0xca202Updated": "Opcode 0xCA (202) updated to report the new multiplier value while maintaining backward-compatible wire format",
"site.help.changelog.fixedSpectator1Follow": "<strong>Fixed spectator #1 follow flickering</strong> — viruses and cells near the viewport edge no longer blink in and out. Root cause: the grouped spectator viewbox had no true hysteresis — the same 600px padding was used for both adding and removing cells, so natural scale/center jitter from the followed player caused edge cells to oscillate between visible/invisible every tick",
"site.help.changelog.implementedAsymmetricHysteresisCells": "Implemented asymmetric hysteresis: cells enter visibility at 600px viewport padding but only leave at 1200px, creating a 600px dead zone that absorbs camera jitter",
"site.help.changelog.addedEmaSmoothingTo": "Added EMA smoothing to spectator scale (15% weight per tick) to dampen per-tick fluctuations from eating, decaying, splitting, and merging",
"site.help.changelog.liveServerStatusEndpoint": "Live server status endpoint: <code>GET /status</code> returns real-time JSON with player count, spectators, uptime, and map scale",
"site.help.changelog.legendmodHomepageNowShows": "LegendMod homepage now shows live ONLINE/OFFLINE badge with dynamic player counts fetched from the game server",
"site.help.changelog.mapScaleIndicatorDisplays": "Map scale indicator: displays current map tier (1/4, 1/2, 1×, 2×, up to 8×) in real time",
"site.help.changelog.statusUpdatesRunOn": "Status updates run on the accept thread with lock-free volatile reads — zero impact on game loop performance",
"site.help.changelog.fixedCellFlickeringBlinking": "Fixed cell flickering/blinking during spectate — MAX_QUERY_NODES increased 8× (8192→65536) to prevent non-deterministic viewport truncation",
"site.help.changelog.viewStateClearedOn": "view_state cleared on every spectate mode transition, fixing one-frame blinks from stale add/update classification",
"site.help.changelog.fixedStaleLeaderboardDisconnected": "<strong>Fixed stale leaderboard</strong> — disconnected players/bots no longer persist on the leaderboard. Server now sends an empty leaderboard packet (count=0) when all players leave",
"site.help.changelog.newEmbedPageGaming": "New <a href=\"/embed.html\">embed page</a> — gaming portals can now embed Expanding Land on their websites with a simple iframe snippet",
"site.help.changelog.maxViewNodesLimit": "MAX_VIEW_NODES limit (16384) prevents OOM crashes during extreme zoom-out while keeping 30× headroom for spectators",
"site.help.changelog.viewportCullingNowSends": "Viewport culling now sends only visible nodes — eliminates FPS drops when zoomed out on large maps",
"site.help.changelog.conditionalLogoutAutoSigns": "Conditional logout: auto-signs out when joining a private server that isn't Expanding Land, preventing opcode 102 conflicts",
"site.help.changelog.loginButtonsFacebookGoogle": "Login buttons (Facebook, Google, Discord) are now disabled on unsupported server types",
"site.help.changelog.fixedCellColorInconsistencies": "Fixed cell color inconsistencies under high bot density by including name/skin data in update packets",
